I walk outside.
The weather in January is very good.
I see a small tea stall on the way.
I go there.
A man makes tea there.
I am very hungry.
"I need a tea," I say.
"Do you have hot pazhampori?" I ask.
"Yes, I have," he says.
He gives me a glass of tea.
He gives a pazhampori with it too.
The pazhampori is very sweet.
I drink the tea.
"How much is it?" I ask.
"Twenty-five rupees," he replies.
I give twenty-five rupees.
